          },
          "span_id": "pdf:aa1ef056169f:page:0018:block:0009:span:0001",
          "text": "It astounds me to think about how far I have gone down the road in 365 days, or how much I have been changed by a place half the globe away from where I come from... It was Friday the 13"
        },
        {
          "language": "en",
          "semantic_line_break_after": false,
          "source_typography": {
            "caps_style": "normal",
            "decorations": [],
            "posture": "italic",
            "vertical_position": "superscript",
            "weight": "normal"
          },
          "span_id": "pdf:aa1ef056169f:page:0018:block:0009:span:0002",
          "text": "th"
        },
        {
          "language": "en",
          "semantic_line_break_after": false,
          "source_typography": {
            "caps_style": "normal",
            "decorations": [],
            "posture": "italic",
            "vertical_position": "baseline",
            "weight": "normal"
          },
          "span_id": "pdf:aa1ef056169f:page:0018:block:0009:span:0003",
          "text": ", 3:29 pm Harvard time that the email came, so phlegmatically that it made me speechless. We hugged; I could feel Mom’s heart beat fast in joy. I thought I would scream, would engage in a frantic dance, would call up everybody I know at 3:30 am in the morning. But Mom once said that, when you have worked hard enough, the happiness of success will come in a composed manner. There was an excitement but also"
        }
